  "id": "DrugBank_DB13092 - MONDO_233",
  "verbalization": "Meclocycline is implicated in the pathogenesis of Japanese Spotted Fever through a chain of indications that ultimately converge on Demeclocycline. The evidence suggests that Meclocycline is linked to Typhus and Brucellosis, both of which are associated with Demeclocycline, which in turn is linked to Japanese Spotted Fever. This suggests a potential mechanistic pathway where Meclocycline may influence the development of these diseases through its interaction with Demeclocycline. The overlapping indications between Meclocycline and Demeclocycline imply a possible functional or pharmacological relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible indirect relationship between Meclocycline and Japanese Spotted Fever, mediated through Demeclocycline, and highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context in drug reutilization efforts.",
